Error Analysis

Summary

The intent classifier (TF-IDF features + Logistic Regression) was trained on 310 hand-written
questions across 8 intents and tested on a held-out 20% (62 questions).

| Measure | Result |
| Accuracy on the held-out test split | 0.65 (40 of 62 correct) |
| Macro F1 | 0.66 |
| 5-fold cross-validation, repeated 3 times | accuracy 0.663 +/- 0.058, macro F1 0.666 +/- 0.057 (folds ranged 0.58 to 0.79) |
| End-to-end test of the full chatbot (42 questions) | 37/42 (88%); 31/35 (88%) on questions not in the training data |

The full chatbot scores higher than the classifier alone because the classifier is backed by a
servant-name recognition step and a few routing rules (explained below).

